ipedia</title><meta name="description" content="Nelson Rolihlahla Mandela (18 July 1918 – 5 December 2013) was a South African anti-apartheid revolutionary, politician, and the first president elected by universal suffrage, serving from 1994 to 1999. A prominent leader in the African National Congress (ANC), Mandela initially pursued nonviolent resistance against the apartheid system&#x27;s racial segregation and disenfranchisement but co-founded its paramilitary wing, Umkhonto we Sizwe (MK), in 1961 to conduct sabotage operations targeting..."/><meta name="author" content="system"/><link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest"/><meta name="keywords" content="Mandela, Madiba"/><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"/><meta name="googlebot" content="index, follow, max-snippet:-1"/><link rel="canonical" href="https://grokipedia.com/page/Nelson_Mandela"/><meta property="og:title" content="Nelson Mandela"/><meta property="og:description" content="Nelson Rolihlahla Mandela (18 July 1918 – 5 December 2013) was a South African anti-apartheid revolutionary, politician, and the first president elected by universal suffrage, serving from 1994 to 1999. A prominent leader in the African National Congress (ANC), Mandela initially pursued nonviolent resistance against the apartheid system&#x27;s racial segregation and disenfranchisement but co-founded its paramilitary wing, Umkhonto we Sizwe (MK), in 1961 to conduct sabotage operations targeting..."/><meta property="og:url" content="https://grokipedia.com/page/Nelson_Mandela"/><meta property="og:site_name" content="Grokipedia"/><meta property="og:locale" content="en"/><meta property="og:image" content="https://grokipedia.com/icon-512x512.png"/><meta property="og:image:width" content="512"/><meta property="og:image:height" content="512"/><meta property="og:image:alt" content="Nelson Mandela"/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:modified_time" content="1970-01-21T09:19:45.901Z"/><meta name="t